r":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T16:54:34-07:00","id":1537534,"title":"","content":"I am presuming they exist somewhere somehow. Possibly in the tellurian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T17:40:40-07:00","id":1537536,"title":"","content":"They'd be super toys and might last all summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T19:42:09-07:00","id":1537538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537528-4d-toys?p=1537534#post1537534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am presuming they exist somewhere somehow. Possibly in the tellurian.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if there's somewhere out in the High Umbra the bigger deal is getting to where they are, and what the rules of that Umbral Realm are, not having to worry about was Spheres govern the hypercubes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T19:49:33-07:00","id":1537539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537528-4d-toys?p=1537538#post1537538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if there's somewhere out in the High Umbra the bigger deal is getting to where they are, and what the rules of that Umbral Realm are, not having to worry about was Spheres govern the hypercubes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a very interesting idea. A hypercube is a cage for spirits?<br /> <br /> <br /> So I'm guessing it does fit with Spirit being Dimensional Science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T20:14:05-07:00","id":1537540,"title":"","content":"I... didn't say anything about hypercubes being a cage for spirits... I was saying that hypercubes would be something you could find in specific spirit Realms because there are Realms where human imagination and thought experiments take on 'real' form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T20:21:34-07:00","id":1537541,"title":"","content":"It's been a long time; but I recall that one of the concepts that was presented in the 1st edition core book was the idea that otherworldly realms could have Sphere ratings, representing the fact that the laws of reality were different there than they were on Earth. Hang in a second while I look that up\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026There it is: page 181. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once a mage leaves the spirit world of the Umbra to enter one of the Realms within it, she becomes subject to the laws of reality within that Realm Each alternate Realm has a rating in each of the nine Spheres. These ratings delineate what is possible within the reality of the Realm; the Realm of Earth has a zero rating in each Sphere. <br /> <br /> For example, the Forces Sphere rating of the Elemental Realm of Electricity is 3. This indicates that it is much easier to manipulate Forces within the static reality of this Realm than it is on Earth. A mage with a Forces rating of up to Rank Three would not be hindered at all by the static reality of the electrical Realm when he performed Forces Magick, nor would he incur Paradox, because such magick does not contradict the reality of the Elemental Realm. <br /> <br /> The ratings of Realms can be positive or negative. For example, a Realm that exists only in two-dimensional space (as in the book <u>Flatland</u>) might have a Correspondence rating of \u20134, reflecting that its reality is much more limited in terms of dimensional space than is Earth's. The same Realm might also have ratings of Entropy \u20132, Forces 0, Life 3, Matter \u20132, Mind 1, Prime \u20132, Spirit 0, and Time 4. All of these ratings reflect the scope of what is possible within the Realm's static reality. </div> </div> </div>We've come a long way since the first edition, and the mechanics described in this section never got any follow-up and in fact never saw the light of day from 2e on. But the <i>premise</i> described here, that Realms on the other side of the Umbra may have different laws of reality than our own, and that those laws can be as drastically different from ours as having a different number of spatial dimensions, seems <i>very</i> much in keeping with the spirit of <b>Mage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T00:23:23-07:00","id":1537546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537528-4d-toys?p=1537541#post1537541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've come a long way since the first edition, and the mechanics described in this section never got any follow-up and in fact never saw the light of day from 2e on. But the <i>premise</i> described here, that Realms on the other side of the Umbra may have different laws of reality than our own, and that those laws can be as drastically different from ours as having a different number of spatial dimensions, seems <i>very</i> much in keeping with the spirit of <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Does it say whether the bonus or malus values indicate a minimum Sphere threshold that is needed to even enter or navigate those realms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537528-4d-toys?p=1537534#post1537534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am presuming they exist somewhere somehow. Possibly in the tellurian.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_crystal\" target=\"_blank\">Time Crystals</a>. One of those things I wish sci-fi would pick up on, they sound like complete esoteric mumbo-jumbo but have been created and observed in laboratories. The tldr is they have a shape in <a href=\"https://archive.ph/20170202102150/http://physics.aps.org/articles/v5/116\" target=\"_blank\">space <i>and </i>time</a>.<br /> <br /> That said, exploring the High Umbra just to find a decorative tesseract for my laboratory table sounds like a thing one of my Mage characters would do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537528-4d-toys?p=1537539#post1537539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes a very interesting idea. A hypercube is a cage for spirits?<br /> <br /> <br /> So I'm guessing it does fit with Spirit being Dimensional Science?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that works if your paradigm sees the Umbrae as extra spatial dimensions (as opposed to, say on a different phase of reality). I would have no trouble allowing a spirit trap effect with a Spirit + Correspondence spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}